  "description": "An experimental rust beetle that can do what normal rust beetles cannot. They are resistant to the flavor of their mutation.",
  "behavior": "It guards the Candy Lab and does not depend on nighttime to appear. It prefers to open distance, flood the ground with acid, and punish you when you try to reclaim space.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "It is especially annoying when other enemies are already active, because it forces you to choose between the acid under your feet and the pressure arriving from the front or the flanks.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "It works best as a zone controller that lets other variants finish targets trapped inside its corrosive puddles. It does not need to chase particularly well if the arena is already fighting for it.",
  "strategy": "Do not hand over ground for free. Close in after the shots and do not let corrosion dictate the entire pace of the fight. If you agree to play at its preferred distance for too long, you are already losing.",
  "environments": [
    "After Unleashing the O.G.R.Rs.",
    "Candy Lab"
  ],
